window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"illaoi","b":"locke","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Locke","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Level 3+","text":"Tentacle setups online — trades taken on your terrain are always yours."},{"when":"Enemy 6 + first item","text":"He dashes out of Leap of Faith and executes you after — hold R until his E is down."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Your R field wins any stationary brawl — he only wins the fights he can leave."},{"text":"Soul Ignition is 18s at rank 1 and he pays for it in his own health — the heal only refunds at the END of the duration, so kill him inside it or land Grievous Wounds before it expires and the refund never arrives.","when":"His W window"}],"wants":{"you":["Fights on planted tentacles only","Landed Tests of Spirit for free stages","His dash baited before Leap of Faith"],"foe":["Sidesteps on Test of Spirit","A dash out of your ult, then the execute","No brawls inside your field, ever"]},"early":"The lane opens honest: no tentacles, no edge. Your job is terraforming — plant tentacles behind the wave, sustain his chip with W trades, and by level 3 every exchange on your terrain leans your way. Levels 4-5 revolve around one skillshot: land Test of Spirit and the stage is yours; miss it and you are both just farming politely.","mid":"His 6-and-first-item window runs a nasty script: you press Leap of Faith, he dashes out, and Purgatory executes you in the wreckage. So flip the order — force his E out with a Test of Spirit or a tentacle chase first, then ult the dash-less assassin. R with his escape still up is a coffin; R onto a spent dash is a coronation.","late":"Two-plus items the deal is simple: any brawl inside your R field you win, and any fight he can exit he wins. Side-lane where the terrain is yours, drop Leap of Faith in chokes or right on his commit, and let the tentacle storm argue for you. He will kite the field's edge — hold W Harsh Lesson to close and keep the fight stationary.","whys":["Level 1 is even — no tentacles planted yet, so it is basic-attack trades on level footing.","Level 2 stays skill — your W trades sustain you through his passive chip.","Level 3 is even: tentacle-backed trades offset his E gap-close — he jumps in, the tentacles answer.","Levels 4-5 stay a skill war that revolves around him dodging Test of Spirit — land it and you win the stage, miss and it is neutral.","Level 6 holds even — the standoff persists while his execute setup is not yet fully online.","First item is Locke's — his E escapes your Leap of Faith and Purgatory executes you afterward, so never burn R without his dash accounted for.","2+ items returns to skill — inside your R field the stationary brawl is yours; the fight is decided by whether he is forced to take it."]});
