window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"illaoi","b":"zaahen","win":["Skill","Illaoi","Illaoi","Skill","Skill","Illaoi","Illaoi"],"spikes":[{"when":"Levels 2-3","text":"Slam-plus-tentacle trades and the Test of Spirit zone — bully him off the wave."},{"when":"Levels 4-5","text":"His 850-range W pull — only fight while standing on your tentacles."},{"when":"First item","text":"Tentacle DPS plus sustain out-brawls him permanently from here."},{"text":"Determination fills from every hit he lands on you and lets him revive once full, so a late fight that looks even is one you have to win twice. Grievous Wounds and a tentacle field planted beside terrain are what make the second kill possible.","when":"Late"}],"wants":{"you":["Trades on tentacle terrain only","Landed E for doubled damage sources","Every fight dragged long — you win long"],"foe":["You pulled off your tentacles","Ult-punished naked commits","Short burst trades, then out"]},"early":"From level 2 you are the bully — Harsh Lesson slams with tentacle follow-up out-trade him, and by 3 the field plus Test of Spirit zones him off the wave. The caveat at 4-5 is his W: it stabs out 850 and pulls you toward him, off your tentacles, on a 14s cooldown. Bully from your setup and never chase past its edge.","mid":"Level 6 is a commit-chicken standoff — Grim Deliverance (R) is 110s at rank 1 against your 120s Leap of Faith, so whoever burns first usually loses. First item resolves it your way. Watch The Darkin Glaive (Q): it is an auto-attack reset that heals him and the recast knocks you up, so the wind-up is your cue to step back, not the cast.","late":"Two-plus items is the punchline: his kit wants extended fights, and extended fights are what Illaoi wins. Buy Grievous Wounds first though — The Darkin Glaive and Grim Deliverance both heal him, and his passive revives him once it fills. Side-lane on terraformed ground, hold W to stick, and E to punish the retreat.","whys":["Level 1 is even — the tentacles are not online yet, so neither kit matters.","Level 2 is Illaoi's: Harsh Lesson slams plus tentacle follow-up out-trade him cleanly.","Level 3 stays yours — the tentacle field plus the Test of Spirit zone owns the lane.","Levels 4-5 even out: his W pulls you 850 units off your tentacles — never fight past the field's edge.","Level 6 is even — Grim Deliverance is 110s, Leap of Faith 120s; whoever commits second wins.","First item is Illaoi: tentacle DPS plus your sustain out-brawls him in every extended trade.","2+ items stays yours — the extended fight his kit wants is exactly the fight you win."]});
